# Keeps the build context (and the image) small. The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`,
# so anything not excluded here ends up in an image layer.

# Dependencies and build output. node_modules matters especially: `npm install`
# runs before `COPY . .`, so copying the host's tree would overwrite the
# container's freshly installed one, possibly with platform-native binaries
# built for the host instead of linux.
node_modules
.next
out
build
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn

# Source data. These CSVs are ~117 MB and are only an input to
# modules/csv_to_parquet_s3.py, which publishes them to the object store as
# Parquet. The dashboard reads that Parquet through the /api/data proxy route, so
# nothing at runtime needs the CSVs.
public/*.csv
public/output*

# Credentials. Without this, `COPY . .` bakes .env into the image, where it stays
# readable in the layer history. Supply these as environment variables instead
# (see compose.yml).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control and tooling
.git
.gitignore
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store

# Python-side utilities; not used at runtime by the Next server
modules
__pycache__
*.pyc

# Local artifacts
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
coverage
Dockerfile
compose.yml
.dockerignore
README.md
CLAUDE.md
